  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The appearance of colour in alkali metal halides is generally due to F-centres. F centers in $\\mathrm{NaCl}$ produce a band of optical absorption towards the blue end of visible\nspectrum, thus the colour appears yellow under transmitted light. On the other hand, $\\mathrm{KCl}$ with $\\mathrm{F}$-centers appears magenta, and $\\mathrm{KBr}$ appears blue.",
    "image": null
  },
